# AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner (CLF-C02) Practice Questions

This repository contains AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner (CLF-C02) practice questions designed to help you prepare for the exam.

## Purpose

The goal of this repo is to provide a simple, focused set of practice questions and study material for AWS Cloud Practitioner topics. It is useful for:
- reviewing core AWS services
- testing your knowledge before the exam
- identifying weak areas
- reinforcing important cloud concepts

## Topics Covered

This repository focuses on key Cloud Practitioner concepts, including:
- cloud computing fundamentals
- AWS core services
- security and compliance
- billing, pricing, and support
- cloud architecture and design
- monitoring, reliability, and scalability

## How to Use This Repository

1. Review the area you want to study.
2. Attempt the practice questions without looking at the answers.
3. Check your understanding and review explanations.
4. Repeat the questions until you feel confident in each topic.

## Suggested Study Approach

- Start with AWS fundamentals and core services
- Focus on security, pricing, architecture, and support topics
- Track your weak areas and revisit them regularly
- Use the questions to reinforce understanding, not just memorization

## Repository Structure

This repository may evolve over time, but it can be organized as follows:

- `questions/` — practice questions
- `answers/` — answer keys or explanations
- `notes/` — study notes and summaries
- `resources/` — links, cheat sheets, and references

## Notes

AWS exam preparation is most effective when you combine:
- practice questions
- conceptual review
- hands-on learning
- repeated revision

## Contributing

If you would like to improve this repository, feel free to add:
- new questions
- explanations
- study notes
- references to AWS documentation

